# Implementation Plan - HOTFIX-013 — Increase Maximum Overlay Transparency to 99.99%

Update the Overlay Visibility transparency system to support floating-point transparency from `0.0%` to `99.99%` (minimum Qt window opacity `0.0001`).

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The transparency model type is updated from integer `int` to float `float` with range `0.0` to `99.99`. Legacy values `> 99.99` (such as `100`) will be automatically normalized to `99.99` on application startup.

## Proposed Changes

### Models & Settings Layer

#### [MODIFY] [settings.py](file:///c:/github/batmanoverlay.com/src/models/settings.py)
- Change `overlay_transparency: float = Field(default=0.0, ge=0.0, le=99.99)`.
- Update `@field_validator("overlay_transparency", mode="before")` to clamp inputs $> 99.99$ to `99.99` while supporting floats and integers.

---

### UI Layer

#### [MODIFY] [overlay_visibility_panel.py](file:///c:/github/batmanoverlay.com/src/ui/overlay_visibility_panel.py)
- Change signal to `transparency_changed = Signal(float)`.
- Scale `QSlider` integer range to `0` .. `9999` (`slider.value() / 100.0` = float transparency).
- Update right endpoint label to `"99.99% (Max Transparency)"`.
- Update text display formatting to format integers as `0%`, `50%`, `99%` and floats as `99.99%`, `94.99%`.
- Update `get_transparency() -> float` and `set_transparency(value: float)`.

#### [MODIFY] [main_window.py](file:///c:/github/batmanoverlay.com/src/ui/main_window.py)
- Update `decrease_opacity()` (`Ctrl+Q`): `new_t = min(99.99, current_t + 5.0)`.
- Update `_on_transparency_changed(transparency_percent: float)`: `opacity = 1.0 - (clamped_t / 100.0)`.
- Update `set_window_opacity(opacity)`: clamp minimum Qt window opacity to `0.0001`.
- Update `_restore_geometry()`: normalize saved transparency to `min(99.99, max(0.0, float(saved_transparency)))`.

